.TH RAND 3
.SH NAME
rand, srand \- random number generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "srand(seed)"
.B "int seed;"
.sp
.B "rand( )"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rand
uses a multiplicative congruential random number generator with
period 2**32 to return successive pseudo-random numbers in the range from
0 to 2**15\-1.
.PP
The generator is reinitialized by calling
.B srand
with 1 as argument.
It can
be set to a random starting point by calling
.B srand
with whatever you like
as argument.
(The current time is not a bad choice).
.sp
